WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.129
Film Courage: From reading your story I think
you said that the late artist formerly known

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:10.940
as Prince gave you advice when you just moved
to Hollywood?

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:17.400
Alex Muñoz, Filmmaker/Founder of FYI Films:
I actually love telling this story so I moved

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.980
to Los Angeles before I got accepted to film
school.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:28.339
And I just figured if I don’t get into USC
or UCLA, I can go be an assistant director

00:00:28.339 --> 00:00:31.419
or get a job with the studios.

00:00:31.419 --> 00:00:38.870
So the second day I was in LA I got an internship
with a company called Propaganda Films and

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:45.350
on my second day on the job a casting director
say “Hey…What’s your name?”

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:52.840
And I said “Alex” And she said “Would
you like to be a stand in for famous rock

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.800
star?”And I said “Well who is it?”

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.180
And she said “I can’t tell you.”

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:00.059
And I said “Nah…I don’t want to be a
stand-in because I want to be behind-the-camera

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:06.680
so I went back to my boss Steven and I said
“Hey, Lisa wants me to be a stand-in for

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.049
a rock star, she won’t tell me who and I
don’t want to do it.

00:01:10.049 --> 00:01:12.911
And he said “Why?”And I said “Because
I want to be a director.

00:01:12.911 --> 00:01:15.210
I don’t want to be in front of the camera,
I want to be behind-the-camera.”

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.520
And he said “You have to do it, you’ve
never been on a professional film set.”

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.740
So I race back and she was on the phone ready
to hire somebody and I said “I’ll do it!

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.740
I’ll do it!”

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:24.740
She said okay.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:33.860
The next day I’m on set and the DP says
“Okay Alex, you can leave now.”

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.910
I turn around and I’m face-to-face with
Prince.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.740
I really wasn’t a big Prince fan at the
time but I was looking down at him and our

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:49.930
noses were like this far apart and I’m like
“Wow, he’s got four inch heels on and

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:53.750
I’m taller than him and he just laughed
and goes “Can we switch places.”

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.149
And I said “Sure.”

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:58.930
We were told not to talk to Prince.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:00.229
They said do not talk to him.

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:02.200
And he talked to me.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:11.920
On day six I got my letter of acceptance from
USC and my roommate got the letter and she

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.519
said “I have something really important
to give you.”

00:02:14.519 --> 00:02:18.690
I said “Okay I’m in Downtown LA on this
music video shoot, can you bring it?”

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:24.450
She gave be the letter, I opened it up and
went to the set and I was really excited,

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.120
I said “I got into USC film school!”

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.159
And everyone started clapping and Prince said
[motions to go over] And I’m like “What?”

00:02:32.159 --> 00:02:33.500
And he goes “Come here.”

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.370
I’m like “What did I do?”

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:39.930
He said “So you are going to be a filmmaker.”

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.140
I said “Yes.”

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.670
He said “Let me hear you say that.”

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.720
I said “Say what?”

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.879
He said “Let me hear you say you are going
to be a filmmaker.”

00:02:47.879 --> 00:02:49.920
And I said “I am going to be a filmmaker.”

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.010
He said “I want you to listen closely.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:57.550
There are four rules I want you to consider
abiding by if you are going to pursue filmmaking

00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:58.550
in this town.”

00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.830
I said “Okay.”

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:04.810
He said “First one, (he pointed up) always
remember God and your the Creator.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.380
Always remember God and your Creator.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:12.770
Number two, always remember where you come
from because when you forget where you come

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:16.230
from you die as an artist.”

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.409
Number three was break the rules.

00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:25.129
If you follow the rules you are going to be
boring and you’re going to fade fast.

00:03:25.129 --> 00:03:30.099
And number four was, always give back.

00:03:30.099 --> 00:03:33.370
You must give back as an artist.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:34.370
And I said “Okay.”

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.710
He said “Repeat what I said.”

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:37.710
And I did.

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:41.530
I call these my four purple cornerstones.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.530
Remember God

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:55.860
Where you come from - never forget

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.129
where you come from

00:03:57.129 --> 00:03:58.129
Break the rules

00:03:58.129 --> 00:04:01.400
And always, always give back

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:05.299
He said grace is really important in your
journey

00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:14.579
After he tested me on the four core principles
he told Rosie his backup singer “Rosie,

00:04:14.579 --> 00:04:18.820
pray for this brother that he does not go
down the dark path.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.860
He needs to stay on the path of light.”

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:31.790
So Rosie took my hands and placed them on
the piano and made a prayer of protection

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:36.980
that I wouldn’t be seduced by the dark side,
what Prince called the fleshly temptations.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.920
And “This is serious, we are praying for
you.”

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.330
And after she prayed, Prince said “Amen.”

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.660
He said “Don’t forget what I told you.”

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.010
And I said “I won’t.”

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:57.130
Imagine that is a priceless encounter, that
cannot be measured.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.470
I had just moved to LA.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:03.710
I’d just finished my undergraduate work
in Santa Barbara.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:08.930
For him to take the time to tell me these
things and share with me his four core principles

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:16.210
and for him to ask his backup singer Rosie
to pray for me, I never forget this.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:25.520
One of the reasons is when I decided to move
forward with FYI Films a non-profit, I rummaged

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:29.960
through my mind I remember Prince saying always
give back and he helped me.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:36.980
I don’t think I’d be talking about FYI
Films if Prince didn’t tell me this about

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:37.980
giving back.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:41.780
Film Courage: Because it seems like all four
things you’ve incorporated (the purple cornerstones)

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:42.780
into your life?

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.250
Alex: I try to.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:50.230
So the second part of the story is when Prince
died the did a tribute concert for him.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:54.100
I called the organizers and said “Hi, my
name is Alex Muñoz.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.480
Prince gave me some really good advice back
in the day.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:57.480
I will do anything.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:03.590
I will sweep the streets, I will sell popcorn,
I will sell popcorn, I’ll do security.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:09.190
I just wanted in my own way pay tribute to
this great artist because he gave me some

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:11.360
good advice I will never ever forget.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.800
So they said “We will call you right back.”

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.710
Two hours later they call me back and they
said “We Googled you and your a filmmaker?

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:21.030
Why don’t you do a film celebrating Prince?”

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.791
I said “The concert is ten days away.

00:06:22.791 --> 00:06:26.030
I can’t possibly make a good enough film.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.251
How about I document it?”

00:06:27.251 --> 00:06:33.090
I went to document this Prince tribute concert.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:39.620
The very first interview I did happened to
be in the very first spot when Prince told

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.270
me the four purple cornerstones.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:47.610
I was like “Oh my gosh, this is where Prince
told me to remember God, remember where you

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:52.350
come from, break the rules and always give
back.”

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.790
I felt really inspired.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:07:01.590
Like my body was trembling because I could
feel his presence in that area where the concert

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:05.580
was right in front of LA City Hall which is
where we shot the video.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:07.490
How uncanny is that?

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:13.270
Then I went out to the audience and interviewed
some people about the concert.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:17.010
Stevie Wonder does this amazing rendition
of Purple Rain.

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:21.780
So I’m trying to go backstage to interview
Stevie and I can’t get to him.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:23.450
The guards are saying “You can’t talk
to Stevie.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:25.460
He doesn’t want to be bothered.”

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:31.600
One of my FYI Film alumni from Hawaii sees
me and says “Hey Alex, what are you doing

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:32.600
here?”

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:38.161
I said “Oh, I think I’ve told you when
I taught FYI Films (when I taught the film

00:07:38.161 --> 00:07:41.451
workshop) that my first experience on a film
set was being Prince’s stand-in?”

00:07:41.451 --> 00:07:43.370
He said “Yes…but what are you doing here?”

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:45.240
I said “I’m doing a documentary.”

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:46.550
He said “Why do you look mad?”

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:49.250
I said “Stevie gave the best performance.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.760
I want to interview him and they won’t let
me get backstage.”

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:53.810
And he said “I can help you.”

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:56.890
I said “That’s really nice of you, but
you can’t help me.”

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:59.430
He said “Alex, I can help you.”

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:01.680
He goes in the back, comes back, he says “Come
on.”

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.040
He takes me to Stevie Wonder.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:08.800
It was Stevie Wonder’s nephew.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.240
So I felt like it was full circle.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:17.960
I mean I’ve got chicken skin right now because
Prince tells me the importance of giving back.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:21.360
I’m there to do a documentary about this
concert.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:28.320
I can’t get to Stevie, it turns out one
of my alumni never told me he was Stevie Wonder’s

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:33.950
nephew, gets me backstage because I believe
I had access to Stevie and all of Prince’s

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:39.370
backup singers and all of Prince’s backup
dancers because if I didn’t teach that FYI

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:43.460
Film workshop in Hawaii, I would have never
met my alumni.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:46.300
Then two years later I see him at this concert
backstage.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.080
That’s Karma.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:51.320
That is “Oh…I’m doing what I’m supposed
to be doing.”

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:56.190
I told him “Why didn’t you ever tell me
you were Stevie Wonder’s nephew?”

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:58.990
He said “I don’t know Muñoz?

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:04.250
I don’t want people to like me just because
we’re related to Stevie.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:08.300
But you earned it because you’ve come to
our birthday parties and our 4th of July parties

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:11.630
and you never asked any questions and you
showed us love anyway.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.910
So okay, now you know.”

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:18.140
So I mean, what a blessing right?

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:22.180
One of my alumni is Stevie Wonder’s nephew
and little did I know that two and a half

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:25.180
years later I would need him to complete my
film.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:29.430
Film Courage: And you’re in the same spot
where you first met Prince on his music video

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:32.110
back in the day in front of LA City Hall

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:36.510
Alex: So my documentary is called PURPLE DOTS.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:41.180
It’s a short film about how I moved to Los
Angeles and Prince gave me this advice and

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:49.030
how 18 years later I’m doing this documentary
at his tribute concert and how my first interview

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:55.770
is in the same spot where I met him and how
it turns out one of my alumni is Stevie Wonder’s

00:09:55.770 --> 00:10:01.150
nephew and then I can get the interviews that
I need.

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:04.380
Alex: That’s its own movie, that’s the
second part of it.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:09.960
Wow…I have a feeling that a lot of stuff
like this happens to you?

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:14.770
That you have this amazing synchronicities
or…maybe I’m wrong?

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:17.830
I just feel like you have a lot of things
like this happen?

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:25.720
Alex: Yes, I think that…I often share this
stuff with people and I put it on my blog,

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:28.960
people say “Why does all of this magical
stuff happen to you?”

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:36.280
I don’t think I see or witness magic more
than anybody else but I do pay attention and

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:42.210
I think I have a heightened sense of awareness
because where I grew up I had to really be

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:46.810
aware of what was going on, who is going to
act out, who is going to become angry, who

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:50.360
is going to become hostile.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:52.340
Because of that I really pay attention.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:59.170
Also, writers and directors have to have super
sharp observational skills so I just pay attention.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:05.160
I don’t think I’m anyone special or I
have the Creator’s favor, I just do pay

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.160
attention.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.560
Film Courage: They always say [regarding]
intuition, we all have it.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:15.010
I think some people have it more developed
even though we all have that ability to be

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:21.390
super or hyper-aware of surroundings and someone’s
mood or intentions.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:31.290
Alex: Right but I never would have imagined
that one of my alumni would have helped me

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:37.620
make a better documentary film and I met him
because I was giving back because Prince asked

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:38.620
me to.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:43.260
Prince challenged me to give back and I did
and as a result I have a better thought about

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.260
him.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:48.590
Film Courage: And it came full circle.

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:51.910
That’s is a powerful story.

